rexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fmodules%2Fms%2Fja%2Fv2%2F1vz0WzVlTANrACdaFSiXqCqcyCyxR7HWpMpheWj8H0w.original.fullsize_3.png?alt=media\"><br/>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"Most Important Selected Qs for JEE Advanced","_book":"68f1ce4cc729e5251bd00430","_chapterKey":"68f1ce4cc729e5251bd00430__68f8d633530ed81e1968d783__68f8d634530ed81e1968d786__68f8d634530ed81e1968d787","_marksId":"67c994b5cc180496584ed210","question":"<strong>Paragraph:</strong>\n<img style=\"width: 420px\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/modules/ms/ja/v2/8YuWXJ2kch_LBYxR7DVqdlsO6ypOBAQAwNaj7xaco0Y.original.fullsize_2.png\"/><br/><strong>Question:</strong>\n<img style=\"width: 450px\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/modules/ms/ja/v2/rJsUcoWtNos_N5X_1SOMuZWobZ24C0jYTaFpIJIFQFc.original.fullsize_2.png\"/><br/>Identify stereochemistry compound 4","explanation":"<img style=\"width: 700px\" src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fmodules%252Fms%252Fja%252Fv2%252F1vz0WzVlTANrACdaFSiXqCqcyCyxR7HWpMpheWj8H0w.original.fullsize_3.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=qxfig138\"/ data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fmodules%2Fms%2Fja%2Fv2%2F1vz0WzVlTANrACdaFSiXqCqcyCyxR7HWpMpheWj8H0w.original.fullsize_3.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fmodules%2Fms%2Fja%2Fv2%2F1vz0WzVlTANrACdaFSiXqCqcyCyxR7HWpMpheWj8H0w.original.fullsize_3.png?alt=media\"><br/>"},{"id":312206,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Alcohols Phenols and Ethers","exam":"Engineering","examName":"Most Important Selected Qs for JEE Advanced","q":"<strong>Paragraph:</strong>\nAn optically active hydrocarbon A has molecular formula $\\mathrm{C}_8 \\mathrm{H}_{88}$. A on monochlorination gives five alkyl halide B to F with their molecular formula $\\mathrm{C}_2 \\mathrm{H}_{12} \\mathrm{Cl}$. B does not undergo dehydrohalogenation on treatment with alcoholic solution of KOH . Treatment of either C or D with alcoholic KOH yields same alkene $\\mathrm{G}\\left(\\mathrm{C}_8 \\mathrm{H}_{16}\\right)$, which on ozonolysis followed by work-up with Zn -dimethyl sulphide gives an optically inactive compound $\\mathrm{C}_6 \\mathrm{H}_{12} \\mathrm{O}$ and ethanal. Also C is enantiomeric, whereas D is distereomeric. E on dehydrohalogenation yields an alkene, which on reductive ozonolysis yields $\\mathrm{H}\\left(\\mathrm{C}_7 \\mathrm{H}_{44} \\mathrm{O}\\right)$, which is optically inactive. H on treatment with $\\mathrm{LiAlH}_4$ yields $\\mathrm{I}\\left(\\mathrm{C}_2 \\mathrm{H}_{16} \\mathrm{O}\\right)$ which can be resolved into enantiomers. F on dehydrohalogenation yields an alkene $\\left(\\mathrm{C}_5 \\mathrm{H}_{16}\\right)$, which on reductive ozonolysis yields $\\mathrm{J}\\left(\\mathrm{C}_3 \\mathrm{H}_{44} \\mathrm{O}\\right)$, which is optically active and has same configuration as that of A. Identify A to J explaining the reactions involved.<strong>Question:</strong>\nIdentify structure of \"A\" compound","options":["<img style=\"width: 120px\" src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fmodules%252Fms%252Fja%252Fv2%252Fmd0ZZhhwcEsy_cEFRhGzzwyAYXZHwuIqvZue1-smKqM.original.fullsize_2.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=qxfig138\"/ data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fmodules%2Fms%2Fja%2Fv2%2Fmd0ZZhhwcEsy_cEFRhGzzwyAYXZHwuIqvZue1-smKqM.original.fullsize_2.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fmodules%2Fms%2Fja%2Fv2%2Fmd0ZZhhwcEsy_cEFRhGzzwyAYXZHwuIqvZue1-smKqM.original.fullsize_